{
 "about": "What Hao-shuo-de must always be able to say: the atoms of meaning (NSM primes), Aristotle's ten categories, and the core grammar and relationships. Each item lists the Hao-shuo-de forms that say it; an atom names the lesson by which one of its forms can be said, and a category or grammar item names the lesson module that teaches it. scripts/check-coverage.js (a gate of npm run check) fails if a form uses a word that isn't in the dictionary, if a taught module is gone, or if no form can be said by that lesson -- so removing or moving a word or module these depend on needs a new form first.",
